title: 'pallet-revive: split the call and instantiate benchmarks by value transfer'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `seal_call`, `seal_instantiate` and `evm_instantiate` now measure the operation
    without value and lose their `t` and `d` arguments. Value transfers have their own benchmarks:
     `seal_call_transfer`, `seal_instantiate_transfer` and `evm_instantiate_transfer`.
    Calls and instantiates without value now cost less, while an instantiate that sends only dust
    pays the full transfer cost, as a call already does.

    `WeightInfo` has these 3 new required methods, so every runtime with its own `pallet_revive`
    weights has to re-run the benchmarks.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
